                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]I streamed this game at [url=https://www.twitch.tv/videos/168032314]twitch[/url].[/b]\n\nMayhem Above is a musical score-attack game set in space. You play as a spaceship and as with other score attack games you have to get as high a score as possible. You do this by grinding the surface of planets, drifting the gravity field of planets, bouncing on the surface of bouncer planets, breaking planets by crashing into them at high speed, going to outer space and \"tackling\", read crashing into, enemies. Everything that generates score increases your combo meter, the more variety the more combo, which is needed to earn a high score amount. \nAs mentioned you can crash into enemies, but the enemies can also shoot at you, so you have to avoid their beams by jumping. If you get hit by an enemy beam your volume, the game's health system, will go down. Luckily you can recover volume by collecting volume cores around the universe. \n\nCompleting a map grants you XP based on your score. Once you have enough XP, you level up. When you level up you get perk points, which will help you gain better control of your spaceship and other nice perks. \n\nThe game uses a simple 2D art-style with a space theme. I had to play the game at the lowest setting, the potato setting, that is what it is actually called. The game is well optimized and will run smoothly on most systems with the correct settings. On high, the game looks absolutely stunning, I can not however run it smoothly at that setting, due to my PC specs.\n\nThe soundtracks fits the game perfectly. The included soundtrack has house, techno and trance music as far as I could tell, but I am not expert on music. The game also has the ability to use your own songs.\n\nIf you like score attack games, I would highly recommend this game. It is fun and it can be challenging when the music gets intense and the screen fills up with enemies.\n\n[code]Submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/semeigaming]Semeicardia Gaming[/url].[/code]",
